A||N||2||MikeSchaefer||How to make my 84 steer like an 85 GT||||5||
Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||09-17-2000||01:30 AM||||Hi,<BR>I used to drive an 85 GT, now I have an 84.  I was wandering what modifications I could make to my 84 to make it steer more like my 85 GT did.  I know there are several differences in parts under there.  Is there a way to swap parts from other fiero's steering  rack (or whatever is needed) to improve my 84?  It just doesn't seem to turn as tightly and accurately.  I have complete access to 87 coupe parts if they are needed. I hope someone can understand what I'm asking  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Thanks,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||JohnnyK||09-17-2000||03:06 AM||||How about just swapping all the '87 steering and suspension parts?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-17-2000||08:17 PM||||Just replacing shocks and struts will do allot for it.<P>check the RPO codes for the 87. unless it has codes indicating one of the special handling packages you're wasting your time.<P>You'd also want to find the 3 turn rack. You need the whole rack.||||reg||1
